From 395092d2a7c8357aa1a377b9966cfc5415237679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shuxueshuxue <98064968+shuxueshuxue@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:20:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gugu: step a conversation back to before one of its prompts
 (_session/revert)

Why: a turn the model service refuses stays in the conversation, so every
later turn is refused with it and the session is lost. Gugu offers
"rewind and edit" on a user message (gugu#7304): the bridge must cut the
conversation back to before that prompt, in place, and continue from there.
The prompt receipt and the replay give each prompt its revert point (the
prompt uuid). _session/revert {sessionId, before, files?} restarts the query
with resume + resumeSessionAt at the last chain entry before the prompt,
under the same session id; files: "restore" first restores the files Claude
edited from that prompt on (Query.rewindFiles; checkpointing is on whenever
file changes are reported, and the receipt says so with files: true).

Upstream: none yet; the ACP has no turn-level rewind (Zed edits a message by
truncating its own thread).

Drop: when the ACP gains a standard turn-level revert that the bridge serves.
